      "content": "The 'payload envelope' concept is useful. I'm concerned about the Chancellor's direct involvement being signaled by the sheer regularity of these 'dummy' communications. \n\nIf an analyst sees a specific node consistently sending 'routine' updates to the inner circle, they'll map the connection regardless of the content. Can we develop a protocol for 'stochastic noise'—basically, how to periodically inject erratic, non-patterned communications from various points in the network to break the signature of the coordination? It has to look like organic, disorganized administrative bloat.",
